-- The vault: the room behind the pipe, and the only level exactly the size of
-- the largest screen — 48x28, which is the Virtual Boy's — so it never scrolls
-- on any console and the whole room is the view. It was 40x28 while a Mega Drive
-- was the widest machine here; widening it is what keeps that property true, and
-- the four columns went on each side in whatever material the edge was made of,
-- so every shelf sits where it did relative to the ones above and below it.
--
-- Its exit does not go back to the overworld. Coming back would restart that
-- level, because entering a scene resets it; going on is what makes finding the
-- pipe worth something.

tile #  wall    solid  vaultwall.svg
tile =  ledge   solid  vaultshelf.svg
tile *  exit           gate.svg
tile .  air            dark.svg

map
